n't willing to  help the people in the Northeast what do  you have to say that  yep well you know look there's time for  political sniping later I think our  focus needs to be it's not political  sniping Katie tours right it's a pretty  simple question of hey it appears you  can be counted on to push for money for  your own constituents but to get in the  way of money for non constituents when  they're all just victims of a natural  disaster in the United States so Katy  tour pushes him and he eventually gives  an answer even though it's an answer  that's been widely debunked for  something like five years running  funding right after that storm I covered  those people many of them just like  those in Houston lost absolutely  everything they owned well Katie Katie  of course that's right and and the  accurate thing to say is that I and a  number of others enthusiastically and  emphatically supported hurricane relief  for sandy hurricane relief and disaster  relief has been a vital federal for a  long long time and it should continue  the problem with that particular bill is  it became a fifty billion dollar bill  yet was filled with unrelated pork  two-thirds of that bill had nothing to  do with Sandy and and what I said then  and still believe now is is that it's  not right for politicians to exploit a  disaster and people are hurting to pay  for their own political wish-list  disaster relief needs to be focused on  the victims of disaster relief and I  supported that for sandy disaster relief  there and I would support that anywhere  there's a major disaster without getting  getting distracted by political  unnecessary pork spending oh that bill  had pork I see well let's evaluate that  assertion oh wait a second it's been  evaluated because Ted Cruz and other  Republicans have been using it for years  and it's just not true  PolitiFact looked at it they looked at  that 2012 superstorm sandy relief bill  and many Republicans use this talking  point some would say well 50 out of the  60 billion dollars in the bill what was  was pork Ted Cruz and others would say  two-thirds of the bill was pork others  said ninety percent of the bill is pork  the truth is its lies and it's not  actually clear exactly how much of the  bill was pork now don't get me wrong Pat  a lot of the bill was pork  of all of these bills is pork it was not  whatever percentage Ted Cruz thinks it  was it's true that there were some funds  in that bill as often is the case that  are for the future mitigation of natural  disasters so after a flood you would  have a bill that includes not only  Direct Relief money for the victims of  that flood but also some money to  strengthen infrastructure in case  there's another flood in the future  because rarely is the most recent  natural disaster the last natural  disaster but there's one other point I  want to make here part of the reason  that the 2012 superstorm sandy relief  bill had pork in it was because you had  red state Republicans like Ted Cruz who  didn't want to support it unless they  got some money for their pet projects so  Ted Cruz is exaggerating number one  number two an incredible hypocrite but  it's his own colleagues that were  demanding the pork and I just think that  even if you're operating from a purely  political perspective and not using your  heart not using empathy wouldn't it make  sense as a senator to support disaster  relief for sandy even though that's not  part of your constituency because you  realize that a natural disaster a  disaster could hit you one day and if  not a hurricane or tornado or a blizzard  or an earthquake and that's just how it  goes it makes sense if you're just a  sort of rational individual it makes  sense if you're just an empathetic  individual it makes sense if you're  gonna try to avoid being a hypocrite who  falls victim to these insane double  standards and to be super clear I'm not  for a second saying that because Ted  Cruz is a [ __ ]  we should punish the people of Texas now  and not give them aid no I think they  should get the aid the same way I  thought that superstorm sandy victims  should get the aid Ted Cruz is the  problem and his constituents are the  ones who need to realize that he's a  problem and maybe vote him out although  it's not particularly likely and  remember Ted Cruz was the guy who was  railing against New York values what  kind of values is he demonstrating here  not the hospitality that we associate  with the south of the United States I'll  say that for sure the video you just  watched was made possible by support  from you please go  to patreon.com slash david pakman show  you can make a pledge of as little as  one dollar per month and every dollar  helps to support the work that we're  doing particularly in light of the  YouTube ad boycott which has been really  bad
 

